course: dictionary
lesson: 8845
title: Shiver: a word with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To shiver means to shake a little, without wanting to, because you are cold, afraid or excited. «The wind made me shiver as I waited for the bus.» The wind is cold, so the shake comes from the cold. A shiver can also be a noun: one small shake is a shiver.
explain: Shiver is often used in phrases. «It sent shivers down my spine» means it made me feel scared or thrilled. Spine is the bone running down your back, so the feeling runs down your body. Check it: put scared into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Shivering also helps your body. When you are cold, tiny muscles shiver quickly and make heat to warm you up. Strong shivering that will not stop can be a warning that you are getting too cold, so get dry, get warm and tell an adult.
fact: Shiver is a verb (shiver, shivers, shivered, shivering) and a noun (a shiver, shivers).
fact: «Shiver» means to shake a little, without wanting to, because of cold, fear or excitement.
fact: «Shivers down my spine» means something made you feel scared or thrilled.
fact: Shivering is a reflex: tiny, fast muscle movements make heat to warm your body.
fact: Bumblebees warm up by shivering their flight muscles, so they can fly on cold spring mornings when honeybees cannot.
exercise: «Her hands began to shiver in the icy wind.» Why did her hands shiver? | Because she was eating a cake | *Because she was cold | Because she was asleep | Because she was painting
exercise: «It sent shivers down my spine.» What does this mean? | It made me feel sleepy | *It made me feel scared or thrilled | It made me cold and wet | It made my back ache from carrying a bag
exercise: Find and copy one word that means to shake a little. | bright | spine | *shiver | sunny
test: Why can bumblebees fly on cold spring mornings? | They wait for the sun to rise and then sleep | *They warm up by shivering their flight muscles | They only fly in summer | They never feel cold at all
test: «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» In this sentence, what does shivers mean? | A loud song | *Small shakes, often from feeling cold or unwell | A sweet drink | A long holiday
exam: What should you do if someone is shivering hard, looks pale and is mumbling? | Put them in a hot bath at once | *Warm them slowly and tell an adult | Give them ice to cool down | Leave them alone so they can sleep
